sentences.l:
But Athena, daughter of aegis-bearing Zeus,
poured down the robe, fine, on her father’s floor,
intricate, which she herself made and toiled at with her hands;

For thus he threatened, the son of Cronus, as he will indeed fulfil it,
to lame, for you two, under the chariot, the swift horses,
and yourselves out of the chariot to throw, and the chariot to break to pieces;

And for them the Hours loosed the fair-maned horses,
and these they tethered at the ambrosial mangers,
and the chariot they leaned against the shining inner wall;
